{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StreamActivityLifecycle","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The activity starts when a named Mac’s picture shows. It keeps running while that Mac stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected without its picture, because iOS pauses a capture card as soon as Headwire leaves the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"screen, which is exactly when the activity becomes visible. It ends when the Mac disconnects or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another Mac takes the screen. One the person swipes away stays away until its Mac leaves the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"screen; one the system ends starts again."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each start and update carries a stale date a minute after it ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/StreamActivityAttributes\/ContentState\/staleDate"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the same situation again re-arms it once 30 seconds have passed, so an activity whose app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was suspended, and so can no longer end it, reads as out of date within a minute. A glance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"picture every 15 seconds re-arms it on the way, so it costs no update of its own then."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/StreamActivityLifecycle\